{"@type":"Dataset","@context":{"@language":"en","@vocab":"https://schema.org/","column":"cr:column","conformsTo":"dct:conformsTo","cr":"http://mlcommons.org/croissant/","dataType":{"@id":"cr:dataType","@type":"@vocab"},"dct":"http://purl.org/dc/terms/","extract":"cr:extract","field":"cr:field","fileProperty":"cr:fileProperty","fileObject":"cr:fileObject","format":"cr:format","includes":"cr:includes","recordSet":"cr:recordSet","sc":"https://schema.org/","separator":"cr:separator","source":"cr:source","transform":"cr:transform"},"conformsTo":"http://mlcommons.org/croissant/1.0","identifier":"https://doi.org/10.1594/PANGAEA.885208","url":"https://doi.pangaea.de/10.1594/PANGAEA.885208","creator":[{"@type":"Person","name":"Ehlke de Jong","familyName":"de Jong","givenName":"Ehlke","email":"djnehl001@myuct.ac.za"},{"@type":"Person","name":"Marcello Vichi","familyName":"Vichi","givenName":"Marcello","email":"marcello.vichi@cmcc.it"},{"@type":"Person","name":"Clinton F W Saunders","familyName":"Saunders","givenName":"Clinton F W"},{"@type":"Person","name":"Mikko J Kotilainen","familyName":"Kotilainen","givenName":"Mikko J"},{"@type":"Person","name":"Hermann Luyt","familyName":"Luyt","givenName":"Hermann"},{"@type":"Person","name":"Stephen P M Peel","familyName":"Peel","givenName":"Stephen P M"},{"@type":"Person","name":"Daniël J Swart","familyName":"Swart","givenName":"Daniël J"}],"name":"Sea ice conditions within the Antarctic Marginal Ice Zone in summer 2016, onboard the SA Agulhas II","publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"PANGAEA","disambiguatingDescription":"Data Publisher for Earth & Environmental Science","url":"https://www.pangaea.de/"},"includedInDataCatalog":{"@type":"DataCatalog","name":"PANGAEA","disambiguatingDescription":"Data Publisher for Earth & Environmental Science","url":"https://www.pangaea.de/"},"datePublished":"2018-01-18","sourceOrganization":{"@id":"https://ror.org/03p74gp79","@type":"Organization","identifier":"https://ror.org/03p74gp79","name":"University of Cape Town"},"additionalType":"dataset","description":"Our knowledge of sea ice variability, which contributes to the detection of the Antarctic climate change trends, stems primarily from remotely sensed information. However, sea ice in the Southern Ocean is characterized by large variability that remains unresolved and limits our confidence on the remotely sensed products. Therefore, the in situ sea ice observations presented (according to the ASPeCt protocol) provide a greater understanding of the Antarctic sea ice environment - on a local scale - and allows us to evaluate remotely sensed products.","abstract":"Our knowledge of sea ice variability, which contributes to the detection of the Antarctic climate change trends, stems primarily from remotely sensed information. However, sea ice in the Southern Ocean is characterized by large variability that remains unresolved and limits our confidence on the remotely sensed products. Therefore, the in situ sea ice observations presented (according to the ASPeCt protocol) provide a greater understanding of the Antarctic sea ice environment - on a local scale - and allows us to evaluate remotely sensed products.","citation":{"@id":"https://store.pangaea.de/Publications/deJong-etal_2018/Erratum_positions.xlsx","@type":["CreativeWork","WebPage"],"identifier":"https://store.pangaea.de/Publications/deJong-etal_2018/Erratum_positions.xlsx","url":"https://store.pangaea.de/Publications/deJong-etal_2018/Erratum_positions.xlsx","name":"Erratum 2018-09-11 position correction"},"spatialCoverage":{"@type":"Place","geo":{"@type":"GeoShape","box":"-69.76667 -0.75367 -57.55 0.94567"}},"temporalCoverage":"2016-12-07T00:00:00/2016-12-10T00:00:00","size":{"@type":"QuantitativeValue","value":603.0,"unitText":"data points"},"variableMeasured":[{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Event label"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Latitude of event"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Longitude of event"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name"